## Decisions locked this session

- **Instruments:** failing/unproven ones get **commented out in place, not deleted**. Scope =
  every LLM-calling utility in the tree. The <$50 calibration budget is **moot** — author chose
  deactivation over proving them ("when I need them I will uncomment them and fix them").
- **Silence is NOT piezoelectric, stores no energy, does not glow, has no hamon.** The entire
  PZT/TENG/spark-drag/draw-strop/ultracapacitor/glowing-hamon/cardiac design is RETIRED.
- **Silence materials:** HE-BMG edge (self-sharpening by shear-banding) + CNT-Titanium yarn spine
  (no crack path, perfect elastic memory) + Covalent Molecular Cross-Linking join (no seam).
- **The blade CONDUCTS; the boron-nitride tsuka/habaki insulate.** That is what lets Kyle fight
  shock rods and arc-fences. His *body* is still vulnerable.
- **NO SAYA. Ever.** Magnetic back mount only — a shaped field holds the blade flat, rotates and
  slides as he moves, never cuts him, releases on the genetic lock. This solves the impossible
  back-draw (arm shorter than a 40-inch blade). Other characters keep their scabbards.
- **STR-CRISPR genetic lock** in the hilt + electro-permanent magnets. Useless to anyone else.
- **Maker's mark:** Dae-jung Seo signed it **prominently** — and someone **ERASED** it. That
  reconciles the togishi scene (#20074: *"Someone erased it… I cannot find the seam"*). The
  erasure IS the lie about how it reached Kyle. Canon only — **not discovered on the page**.
- **Dae-jung Seo: status `unknown`, NOT deceased.** Legendary smith, late 2100s. No record of his
  death — deliberately reserved as material for a future novel. Do not resolve his fate in BCODA.
- **#20211 throat strike uses the mune** (spine), not a scabbard.
- **THE OBSERVATION RULE** (outranks everything): the 5D entity is future Kyle; it can act only
  because **Kyle never observes it**; the **reader** is the sole observer and the collapse happens
  outside the story → no paradox. **Kyle may NEVER learn the entity is himself.**

